BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC State African American Cultural Center
DTSTAMP:20260722T033519Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53374358673631
DTSTART:20260917T213000Z
DTEND:20260917T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the African American Cultural Center (AACC) for the EQUIP 
 orientation and to learn how this year-long initiative can help you create
  the college experience you want in and outside of the classroom. EQUIP st
 ands for Empower\, Question\, Understand\, Initiate and Partner. The initi
 ative is designed to help first-year students:\n\nEmpower themselves to cr
 eate the college experience they want.Question everything to build habits 
 for life-long learning.Understand themselves and what they need to be succ
 essful.Initiate action and be proactive to find resources.Partner with oth
 ers to build a network of care and community.As an EQUIP participant\, you
  will:\n\nEngage in monthly check-ins with a dedicated staff member.Attend
  learning labs and AACC signature events.Work with an embedded AACC counse
 lor.Attend EQUIP special programs.Develop skills in self-awareness\, resil
 ience and help-seeking.EQUIP supports first-year students at NC State in c
 ultivating self-awareness\, community and resilience through AACC signatur
 e events\, wellness activities and proactive campus resource engagement.\n
 \nContact Andaiye Qaasim\, assistant director of the AACC\, at aaqaasim@nc
 su.edu if you have questions.
GEO:35.785108;-78.674529
LOCATION:Witherspoon Student Center\, African American Cultural Center Room
  356
SUMMARY:EQUIP Leadership Program Orientation for First-Year Students
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/equip-leadership-program-for-
 first-year-students
CATEGORIES:Student Life
CATEGORIES:Information Session
CATEGORIES:High-Impact Experiences
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC State African American Cultural Center
DTSTAMP:20260722T033519Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53374475146832
DTSTART:20260924T213000Z
DTEND:20260924T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:Are you ready to thrive at NC State? If so\, join the African A
 merican Cultural Center (AACC) for the EQUIP fall academic workshop. The w
 orkshop is designed to help first-year students master the academic transi
 tion to NC State. Co-facilitated with campus partners and peer leaders\, t
 his interactive session will focus on practical skills\, such as college-l
 evel study strategies\, major exploration\, syllabus navigation and buildi
 ng effective relationships with faculty and advisors. \n\nEQUIP is a year-
 long initiative that supports first-year students as they cultivate self-a
 wareness\, resilience\, and community. Through EQUIP\, you will:\n\nEmpowe
 r yourself to own your academic and personal journey.Question and develop 
 lifelong learning habits.Understand your strengths and what drives your su
 ccess.Initiate proactive connections with campus resources.Partner with pe
 ers and mentors to build a network of care.Participants will have access t
 o dedicated staff check-ins\, an embedded AACC counselor and exclusive spe
 cial events designed just for them.\n\nContact Andaiye Qaasim\, assistant 
 director of the AACC\, at aaqaasim@ncsu.edu if you have questions.
GEO:35.785108;-78.674529
LOCATION:Witherspoon Student Center\, African American Cultural Center (Roo
 m 356)
SUMMARY:EQUIP Academic Workshop
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/equip-academic-workshop
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Training
CATEGORIES:Student Life
CATEGORIES:High-Impact Experiences
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC State African American Cultural Center
DTSTAMP:20260722T033519Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53391555009737
DTSTART:20260925T180000Z
DTEND:20260925T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the African American Cultural Center as it celebrates Hara
 mbee! and 55 years of the African American Cultural Center and its legacy 
 of fostering community\, connection and student success at NC State.\n\nHa
 rambee! is designed to connect the Wolfpack community with a wide array of
  resources and services available on and off campus. By strengthening rela
 tionships across the university and beyond\, the program promotes academic
  achievement and personal growth.\n\nTogether\, we will celebrate our shar
 ed commitment to excellence\, belonging and community.
GEO:35.785221;-78.675064
LOCATION:Harris Field
SUMMARY:Harambee!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/harambee-9582
CATEGORIES:Community Events
CATEGORIES:Student Life
END:VEVENT
